The argument of `spawn` is `Mutex<Mutex<Counter>>`, which reaches a `Mutex` through `m.guard.value`: a `Mutex` reaches a task as its argument or as a field of the class its argument is, never deeper, so which tasks share a lock is a question the checker can answer; hand the task the `Mutex` itself, `s.spawn(outer, m.guard.value, done, 0)`, and declare its parameter a `Mutex` of the same data
